  <h1>Nicolás Medina Sánchez</h1>

<div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; justify-content:space-between; gap:2rem; margin-bottom:2.2rem;">
  <div class="epigraph" style="margin-bottom:0;">
    <p>Toute séparation est un lien.</p>
    <cite>Simone Weil, <em>La pesanteur et la grâce</em></cite>
  </div>
  <img src="/website/foto.jpeg" alt="Nicolás Medina Sánchez"
       style="width:150px; height:150px; object-fit:cover; border-radius:50%; flex-shrink:0;">
</div>

<p class="body-text">
  By some vicissitude of fate I ended up as a postdoc at the Research Center for Quantum Information 
  (<a href="https://quantum.physics.sk/rcqi/">RCQI</a>) of the Slovak Academy of Sciences in Bratislava. 
  Before that, I was a <em>Doktorand</em> at the University of Vienna under the one and only 
  <a href="https://dakic.univie.ac.at/">Borivoje Dakić</a>. Proud alumnus of the Universidad Nacional de Colombia, 
  where I worked with <a href="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Thomas-Dittrich">Thomas Dittrich</a> suffering physics and with 
  <a href="https://avillavecesn.net/">Andrés Villaveces</a> attempting mathematics.
</p>

   <p class="body-text">
    I work on axiomatic reconstructions of physical theories from somehow meaningful
    principles. Most of this has gone into quantum theory, spacetime, and the collective
    behaviour of individual systems. At some point I also spent time with nonlinear dynamics and chaos in driven crystals,
    and with contextuality in its categorical formulation, asking how contexts contain and overlap each other, cohomologically speaking...
  </p>

  <p class="body-text">
    Interested mainly in combinatorics and topology. Though I have indulged myself into
	    sheaf theory, Hopf algebra representations, Manin's quantum linear spaces (AKA quadratic algebras), different flavours of logic, 
		and the back-and-forth between metric and measure structures,
    among other things.
  </p>

  <p class="body-text">
    My favourite topics to talk about over a pint are phenomenology, cybernetics, studium/punctum duality, dissipative structures, hauntology, propensism, 
    anticipatory systems and gothic materialism.
  </p>


